       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is double the 3,200 mg/day maximum in the FDA labeling for prescription ibuprofen. The single dose of 1,600 mg is also above the usual 800 mg per-dose maximum. Normal kidney and liver function don't change that ceiling, and at this dose the risks include GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention.\n\nCommon regimens that stay within the limits:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **400\u2013800 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours** (maximum 3,200 mg/day)\n\nIf you meant 1,600 mg as a single dose or as a total daily amount, tell me which and I'll enter it. If you want 1,600 mg four times daily despite the labeled maximum, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note documenting the intent."
